      "species_basis": "confirmed by Queensland Heritage Register listing and Wikipedia",
      "age_estimate": "taller tree ~190 years, smaller ~140 years (per Queensland Heritage Register citation)",
      "note": "A genuinely compact pair, one site, historically significant (marks the original Stewart Farmhouse site, among the earliest non-Indigenous settlement in Bald Hills; hoop pine logging was one reason for the Moreton Bay penal settlement). BLOCKED ON ACCESS ONLY, not on quality: the pair stands 'at the end of the school's main driveway, framing the entrance to the Administration Building' of St Paul's Anglican School, a 51-hectare private campus at 34 Strathpine Road; no source found stating the driveway or entrance is open to the public without a school reason to be there. Per the school-grounds rule this stays a lead rather than a block: if a future pass finds evidence of genuine public access (a public path, visibility from Strathpine Road itself, stated open days) it can ship. Not researched further in this pass (checked 2026-09-01)."
