      "species_basis": "genus read from the tree's own name; ask the reader which species",
      "reason": "not a collectible point: the Queensland Heritage listing covers three separate fig groupings (5 trees at Normanby Fiveways, 7 at Marshall Park, 3 at Prospect Terrace) strung along a full kilometre of Kelvin Grove Road, with no single obvious place to stand, the same 'avenue' shape as the rejected Plane Trees of La Rambla precedent (checked 2026-09-01, source: en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kelvin_Grove_Fig_Trees_and_Air_Raid_Shelter). If wanted later, the Prospect Terrace corner alone (3 weeping figs plus the WWII air raid shelter, now a bus shelter, with a fig branch grown onto its roof) is a narrower, genuinely compact candidate that was not separately researched in this pass."
